course: dictionary
lesson: 12302
title: Copycat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A copycat is a person who copies what someone else does, says or wears. «Sam wore a red hat, so Lily wore a red hat too. "Copycat!" said Tom.» Tom is teasing Lily because she copied Sam.
explain: Look for clues in the words around copycat. The word has copy in it, and the sentence shows someone doing the same thing as someone else. Ask yourself: did one person do what another person did first?
explain: The word can also describe a thing. «The new shop sold a copycat version of our cereal.» Here copycat means the cereal copies one that already exists. Try your meaning in the sentence: "copying" fits, so you are on the right track.
fact: A copycat is a person who copies what someone else does, says or wears.
fact: «Copycat!» is a teasing word that children often shout in the playground.
fact: As an adjective, copycat describes something that copies something that happened or existed before, like a copycat crime.
fact: A copycat crime is done in the same way as an earlier, well-known crime.
fact: Copycat is an informal word, so you will hear it in talk more than in formal writing.
exercise: «Sam wore a red hat, so Lily wore one too. Tom said, "Copycat!"» What does copycat mean here? | A person who runs very fast | A person who forgets things | *A person who copies what someone else does | A person who sells cats
exercise: «The new shop sold a copycat version of our cereal.» What does copycat describe? | Very cheap and very old | Hidden under the table | *Copying something that already exists | Made of real cats
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means someone who copies: «Don't be a copycat, Ruby. Make your own picture.» | *copycat | Ruby | picture
test: «The police said the robbery was a copycat crime, done just like the one last month.» What is a copycat crime? | A crime that happens with a cat in it | A crime where nothing is stolen | *A crime done in the same way as an earlier crime | A crime that happens only in the morning
test: Mia tells her friend, «Stop being a copycat!» What is she asking him to do? | Stop eating cake | Stop running away | *Stop copying what I do | Stop singing loudly
exam: In «The copycat shoes sold out quickly», what kind of word is copycat? | Verb | Noun | Adverb | *Adjective
